I suppose I should be getting back to work.

00:14:50.450 --> 00:14:50.830
Yes, well.

00:14:57.740 --> 00:14:59.160
You are going to ruin your appetite.

00:15:00.350 --> 00:15:02.370
Wow, you said that just like my mom.

00:15:02.640 --> 00:15:04.890
Yeah, well, we all get the same training tapes.

00:15:05.790 --> 00:15:06.490
Canola's better, right?

00:15:06.710 --> 00:15:07.550
Yeah, it works for me.

00:15:07.760 --> 00:15:08.320
Do you cook?

00:15:08.700 --> 00:15:09.220
Hell no.

00:15:09.710 --> 00:15:11.330
For some reason, I love cooking shows.

00:15:11.410 --> 00:15:12.670
Can't get enough of that iron chef.

00:15:13.410 --> 00:15:16.590
I like watching Oleg do it, but I feel no need to try it myself.

00:15:17.390 --> 00:15:18.960
Well, I like cooking for Jake.

00:15:19.480 --> 00:15:22.360
Sam only gets excited if I make something in the Frank and Beans family,

00:15:22.440 --> 00:15:24.160
but your brother will eat anything.

00:15:24.380 --> 00:15:24.540
Yeah.

00:15:24.820 --> 00:15:25.800
I've tried recipes on him.

00:15:25.820 --> 00:15:27.780
I wasn't even sure I'd want to eat, and he's always a trooper.

00:15:30.160 --> 00:15:31.220
You're in love with him, aren't you?

00:15:33.020 --> 00:15:33.320
What?

00:15:33.830 --> 00:15:35.650
It's okay. I'm not going to say anything to him.

00:15:35.770 --> 00:15:38.660
But, um, you might want to at some point.

00:15:39.250 --> 00:15:41.670
I don't think that we're there yet, or I don't know if we are.

00:15:42.740 --> 00:15:43.780
Let's just see what happens.

00:15:44.020 --> 00:15:46.280
Yeah, well, I'd tell him sooner rather than later if I were you.

00:15:47.280 --> 00:15:49.660
That way he might bring you back to L.A. when he comes home.

00:15:50.840 --> 00:15:51.900
Look, um, so here's the deal.

00:15:52.000 --> 00:15:54.840
And, by the way, I feel like a total ass now for doing it.

00:15:54.920 --> 00:15:58.410
But, uh, I kind of told Jake to break up with you.

00:16:01.690 --> 00:16:03.290
Really? That was sweet of you.

00:16:04.330 --> 00:16:08.840
Hold up. Wait, let me explain.

00:16:10.400 --> 00:16:13.140
I know for a fact that Jake's going to wind up moving back to L.A.

00:16:13.550 --> 00:16:15.650
I told him to break up with you to save you the heartache.

00:16:15.870 --> 00:16:17.310
So technically, I was looking out for you.

00:16:18.340 --> 00:16:20.560
Why do you think he's moving back to L.A.? Did he say something to you?

00:16:20.660 --> 00:16:22.940
No, I just know he doesn't belong here. The guy sticks out.

00:16:24.100 --> 00:16:25.820
You know, he doesn't stick out. He stands out.

00:16:26.080 --> 00:16:29.740
And you've only been here for one day, so maybe you should keep your opinions to yourself.

00:16:30.410 --> 00:16:38.450
He's broke Nina. Look, I've been doing his books and he's not making a third of what he used to so he's not standing out enough.

00:16:38.920 --> 00:16:46.070
You know what I mean? No, I don't. He's got malpractice costs, med school loans, plus he's got his payments on his place in LA.

00:16:46.520 --> 00:16:51.440
He still has a place there? Look, I came out here to help him and I'll be honest,

00:16:51.620 --> 00:16:57.060
I didn't think I'd give a rats about you, but now that I've met you, I like you, Nina.

00:16:57.910 --> 00:16:59.970
I mean, I don't know if I see you two in a...

00:17:00.030 --> 00:17:02.350
for the long haul, but, uh, who knows?

00:17:04.200 --> 00:17:06.740
Anyway, I just, uh, I wanted to give you the heads up.

00:17:07.560 --> 00:17:18.090
What about this one?

00:17:18.500 --> 00:17:19.500
Uh, it's a little dull.

00:17:19.720 --> 00:17:21.180
I mean, you want to look hot, don't you?

00:17:21.440 --> 00:17:22.900
Damn, girl, three days with Topher

00:17:22.900 --> 00:17:24.000
and suddenly you're Paris Hilton?

00:17:24.380 --> 00:17:26.210
Two and a half?

00:17:26.450 --> 00:17:27.850
Lunch doesn't count as a whole date.

00:17:28.520 --> 00:17:29.970
I just don't know if Ephraim should start.

00:17:30.000 --> 00:17:33.860
off with more of a bang yes but we're not technically starting it's more like we almost

00:17:33.860 --> 00:17:37.580
got cancelled then everyone decided that they loved us so we got picked up for another season

00:17:37.580 --> 00:17:43.110
we watch way too much tv besides it's going to take a while for ephrem and i to get completely

00:17:43.110 --> 00:17:49.020
back to normal i don't want to freak him out with an overly sexy dress okay that's fair but i really

00:17:49.020 --> 00:17:52.800
don't think it's going to take as long as you think i mean if you can get through this this

00:17:52.800 --> 00:17:58.140
was like a greek tragedy it should be easy peasy from here on out okay don't say anything obviously

00:17:58.950 --> 00:17:59.310
Obviously.

00:18:00.320 --> 00:18:03.650
But I'm starting to feel like Ephraim and I could really work, you know, like forever.

00:18:03.970 --> 00:18:07.430
I mean, you're right, we have been through everything horrible that could possibly happen,

00:18:07.450 --> 00:18:09.050
and we're still madly in love with each other.

00:18:09.210 --> 00:18:11.290
And I know we're still in high school.

00:18:11.430 --> 00:18:13.700
So? So? That's when my parents met.

00:18:13.980 --> 00:18:15.880
Same as yours. They're all still together.

00:18:17.340 --> 00:18:18.840
Yeah, but things were different back then.

00:18:19.000 --> 00:18:22.840
Why? You and Ephraim just went through your first big cycle, but it was only your first.

00:18:22.920 --> 00:18:26.160
You're gonna have a million more, and I will be there to take care of your grandchildren

00:18:26.160 --> 00:18:27.600
when you need a little private nookie time.

00:18:27.740 --> 00:18:29.980
Oh, ew. I've seen your citizens make out.

00:18:30.000 --> 00:18:31.700
I have heard the stories about your grandma.

00:18:32.180 --> 00:18:34.760
Okay, you have officially lost your maid of honor status.

00:18:37.190 --> 00:18:39.950
Well, you're not pregnant, but no real surprise there, right?

00:18:40.290 --> 00:18:46.720
I'm sorry I figured you knew.

00:18:47.950 --> 00:18:49.810
If we knew, we wouldn't be here, Doctor.

00:18:51.030 --> 00:18:52.710
I'll admit, I am surprised.

00:18:53.170 --> 00:18:54.130
I truly thought...

00:18:55.430 --> 00:18:56.090
Well, never mind.

00:18:58.290 --> 00:18:59.970
Well, hey, if you guys are interested in...

00:19:00.000 --> 00:19:04.020
conceiving. There's a lot of stuff we can try. We should just get a sample from you, Hal, just to

00:19:04.020 --> 00:19:09.740
check sperm count motility. Yes, you needn't concern yourself with my motility, doctor. And I don't believe

00:19:09.740 --> 00:19:15.380
we require any further assistance. Maybe we do. For the last few weeks, you've been telling me that

00:19:15.380 --> 00:19:19.700
my symptoms were all stress-related. Yes, and you were convinced that you were pregnant. I am not

00:19:19.700 --> 00:19:26.900
the doctor. Glad you finally understand that. Uh, anywho, I was actually trying to cut out of here

00:19:26.900 --> 00:19:29.880
early today. My brother's in town visiting. Tell me something, Dr. Hartman.

00:19:30.000 --> 00:19:34.560
If I were a patient of yours and I came to you complaining of back problems, constant fatigue...

00:19:34.560 --> 00:19:35.340
Don't exaggerate, Rose.

00:19:35.480 --> 00:19:35.880
Nausea.

00:19:36.120 --> 00:19:37.280
Uh, okay.

00:19:37.520 --> 00:19:41.200
Well, it's a little early, but it might be menopause.

00:19:42.300 --> 00:19:46.340
Your whole body can get thrown all out of whack, even fighting off a localized issue.

00:19:46.640 --> 00:19:51.180
But since you're having back troubles, I might also want to rule out a compression fracture, osteoporosis.

00:19:51.400 --> 00:19:51.940
Yes, yes, yes, yes.

00:19:51.980 --> 00:19:53.120
I can do the x-ray.

00:19:53.200 --> 00:19:55.240
Excuse me, but I asked Dr. Hartman.

00:19:56.580 --> 00:19:59.120
Where on earth is this hostility coming from, Rose?

00:19:59.180 --> 00:19:59.960
You can't be upset with the result.

00:20:00.000 --> 00:20:02.180
since you made it abundantly clear how little you want.

00:20:02.240 --> 00:20:06.060
Don't even presume to understand how I am feeling, Harold Abbott.

00:20:06.140 --> 00:20:07.420
You certainly implied...

00:20:07.420 --> 00:20:09.380
No, you inferred, as you so often do,

00:20:09.500 --> 00:20:11.120
all I did was express my concern

00:20:11.120 --> 00:20:13.000
at the prospect of being pregnant again.

00:20:13.220 --> 00:20:14.720
All righty, then. I'm just gonna...

00:20:14.720 --> 00:20:16.660
That is most certainly not the impression you gave.

00:20:16.780 --> 00:20:18.380
You let me presume that I was the only one

00:20:18.380 --> 00:20:20.700
with any hopeful interest in the idea you should have just said.

00:20:20.780 --> 00:20:22.940
You were busy shopping for strollers.

00:20:23.080 --> 00:20:24.680
Online! And it took all of two minutes.

00:20:24.900 --> 00:20:26.800
Not as if I drove the minivan to Sears for the day.

00:20:26.800 --> 00:20:27.780
So now you want a minivan?

00:20:28.680 --> 00:20:29.700
Oh, just forget it.

00:20:30.440 --> 00:20:31.440
I have to get back to the office.

00:20:31.880 --> 00:20:33.400
I've missed enough work as it is.

00:20:38.040 --> 00:20:39.000
Just shut up.

00:21:03.480 --> 00:21:07.190
Uh-huh. Nice to see you still recognize quality advice when you hear it.

00:21:07.590 --> 00:21:08.510
What are you talking about now?

00:21:10.070 --> 00:21:12.010
You and Amy back on the love train.

00:21:12.250 --> 00:21:15.650
I heard about your big date, and I'd like to think that I had a little bit to do with that.

00:21:15.810 --> 00:21:18.070
Well, first of all, there's no love train, okay?

00:21:18.230 --> 00:21:19.770
And it's not even technically a date.

00:21:19.850 --> 00:21:21.510
We're just hanging out, you know, seeing how it goes.

00:21:22.440 --> 00:21:25.350
Really? Oh?

00:21:26.290 --> 00:21:28.990
What do you mean? Oh, what do you say? Oh, like that.

00:21:29.130 --> 00:21:29.930
What is that supposed to be?

00:21:30.090 --> 00:21:31.590
Does Amy know that it's not a date?

00:21:32.280 --> 00:21:35.060
Because the mood around here has basically been that you two have moved back into Coupleville.

00:21:35.340 --> 00:21:36.860
What? No. Did she say that?

00:21:37.000 --> 00:21:37.440
Pretty much.

00:21:37.660 --> 00:21:38.740
But I didn't even... I...

00:21:38.740 --> 00:21:40.760
Oh, man.

00:21:42.900 --> 00:21:45.880
Look, it's not like I don't miss her. I do miss her.

00:21:45.960 --> 00:21:49.100
But I just... I can't... I can't be a boyfriend again.

00:21:49.220 --> 00:21:50.980
I'm not ready yet. Too much has happened.

00:21:51.100 --> 00:21:52.540
You know, I need to figure some things out.

00:21:52.740 --> 00:21:55.940
Well, you probably should have told her all that stuff before she bought the dress.

00:21:56.340 --> 00:21:57.340
She went shopping?

00:21:57.980 --> 00:21:59.980
I said...

00:22:00.480 --> 00:22:01.080
Let's hang out.

00:22:01.220 --> 00:22:03.630
Dude, you don't have to pop an aneurysm over this, okay?

00:22:03.910 --> 00:22:05.770
All you got to do is say something to her,

00:22:06.010 --> 00:22:07.190
let her know where you're coming from,

00:22:07.330 --> 00:22:08.130
buy yourself a little time.

00:22:08.250 --> 00:22:08.750
Yeah, you're right.

00:22:09.480 --> 00:22:09.980
I can do that.

00:22:10.640 --> 00:22:12.320
Oh, and wherever you land, you better do it fast

00:22:12.320 --> 00:22:14.580
because Amy knows what she wants, and it's you.

00:22:18.360 --> 00:22:19.560
You ready to go?

00:22:24.960 --> 00:22:25.640
Kids, have fun.

00:22:26.160 --> 00:22:28.760
So, Andy, rumor has it you're the big celebrity around here.

00:22:28.920 --> 00:22:29.960
The little bar is so pretty.

00:22:30.910 --> 00:22:32.010
Oh, listen to him.

00:22:32.320 --> 00:22:34.900
The cover of time counts as pole vault height.

00:22:35.440 --> 00:22:37.520
He's no Vince Vaughn, but he's the best we can do out here.

00:22:38.790 --> 00:22:40.610
Cocktails at 5.30, dinner at 6.30?

00:22:40.790 --> 00:22:42.630
It's been a while since I've eaten this early.

00:22:42.860 --> 00:22:44.400
I mean, back home, the good restaurants

00:22:44.400 --> 00:22:45.440
don't even open till 7.

00:22:45.920 --> 00:22:47.700
Well, we have to get to bed early around here

00:22:47.700 --> 00:22:49.180
so we can get up and milk the cows.

00:22:51.280 --> 00:22:51.840
She's kidding.

00:22:51.960 --> 00:22:52.820
She doesn't have any cows.

00:22:54.130 --> 00:22:55.370
Although he does have a point.

00:22:55.780 --> 00:22:57.180
The pace of things in this town does

00:22:57.180 --> 00:22:58.280
take a little getting used to.

00:22:58.480 --> 00:22:58.840
Really?

00:23:00.000 --> 00:23:00.760
I know you're so bored.

00:23:01.150 --> 00:23:02.150
Do I smell cumin?

00:23:02.330 --> 00:23:03.090
I love cumin.

00:23:03.190 --> 00:23:03.970
That's not what I meant.

00:23:04.760 --> 00:23:06.290
Andy, help me out here.

00:23:06.490 --> 00:23:08.530
You must have had a hard time making the transition

00:23:08.530 --> 00:23:09.230
from New York.

00:23:09.980 --> 00:23:11.400
Yes, Andy, why didn't you help Jake out here?

00:23:11.560 --> 00:23:13.400
No, no, it's paprika.

00:23:13.500 --> 00:23:14.420
That's what it is.

00:23:14.740 --> 00:23:15.900
They're both reddish.

00:23:15.940 --> 00:23:16.700
I get the two confused.

00:23:16.920 --> 00:23:17.740
You watch The Iron Chef?

00:23:17.920 --> 00:23:18.240
I do.

00:23:18.320 --> 00:23:19.120
I love that show.

00:23:19.360 --> 00:23:21.380
You notice how the guy looks exactly like you?

00:23:21.920 --> 00:23:22.300
Sorry.

00:23:22.890 --> 00:23:23.130
It slipped.

00:23:23.630 --> 00:23:27.020
Damn it.

00:23:27.510 --> 00:23:28.010
You all right?

00:23:28.150 --> 00:23:28.430
No.

00:23:28.570 --> 00:23:29.690
I just burned my hand.

00:23:30.190 --> 00:23:30.530
Come here, come here.

00:23:31.090 --> 00:23:31.730
I'm fine.

00:23:31.850 --> 00:23:32.510
It's just your kitchen.

00:23:32.630 --> 00:23:33.850
It was stupid to cook over here.

00:23:34.010 --> 00:23:35.390
Well, we could have done your place.

00:23:36.780 --> 00:23:37.360
I'm sorry.

00:23:37.480 --> 00:23:39.960
You know what, I am, uh, I'm just exhausted.

00:23:40.260 --> 00:23:41.640
And to tell you the truth, I'm not that hungry.

00:23:41.840 --> 00:23:44.560
So, um, why don't you guys just have a boys' night?

00:23:44.780 --> 00:23:45.600
No, I wouldn't.

00:23:45.820 --> 00:23:48.840
No, seriously, that way you guys could all eat at eight

00:23:48.840 --> 00:23:51.220
or nine or whenever, and then you could all pretend

00:23:51.220 --> 00:23:52.220
that you're back in a big city.

00:23:57.600 --> 00:23:57.920
So?

00:24:00.000 --> 00:24:00.780
Any good bars in this town?

00:24:01.410 --> 00:24:03.690
Louise should be back with that x-ray in just a few minutes.

00:24:04.720 --> 00:24:05.160
That's fine.

00:24:05.400 --> 00:24:15.440
What do you want from me, Rose?

00:24:15.780 --> 00:24:18.300
Should I continue in my attempt to understand

00:24:18.300 --> 00:24:19.600
what is going through that head of yours,

00:24:19.600 --> 00:24:21.860
or would you prefer to be left alone?

00:24:22.000 --> 00:24:23.460
Frankly, I'm at a loss.

00:24:24.450 --> 00:24:26.210
I don't know what's wrong with me, Harold.

00:24:27.050 --> 00:24:27.570
The x-ray?

00:24:28.030 --> 00:24:29.150
Oh, no, I'm sure that'll be fine.

00:24:29.250 --> 00:24:29.970
No, I don't mean that.

00:24:30.060 --> 00:24:34.080
I mean, you were right, and initially I didn't want another child.

00:24:34.570 --> 00:24:36.750
It just seemed like such an exhausting prospect.

00:24:37.360 --> 00:24:38.120
But then I...

00:24:39.650 --> 00:24:40.110
Then what?

00:24:41.650 --> 00:24:44.750
Well, once I got past my anxieties about the actual pregnancy

00:24:44.750 --> 00:24:51.200
and started thinking about the possible baby, I really wanted her.

00:24:52.880 --> 00:24:53.660
Her, was it?

00:24:54.420 --> 00:24:57.080
Appropriately fingered and told, but I was hoping for a girl.

00:24:58.020 --> 00:24:58.320
See?

00:25:00.960 --> 00:25:03.340
To want another child at our age? I don't know.

00:25:04.910 --> 00:25:06.370
Gina Davis seems to be doing okay.

00:25:08.320 --> 00:25:09.280
I have to be honest with you, Rose.

00:25:09.600 --> 00:25:13.520
I never felt more useful in this world than the day I became a father.

00:25:14.020 --> 00:25:17.040
I never saw more clearly what I was put on earth for.

00:25:17.400 --> 00:25:21.210
We raised two wonderful children with good hearts.

00:25:21.520 --> 00:25:23.200
The girl's going to Princeton, for heaven's sake.

00:25:23.340 --> 00:25:24.400
I would say we did fantastic.

00:25:26.580 --> 00:25:29.970
You know, Rose, I was reading this article about...

00:25:30.000 --> 00:25:33.000
this woman in Budapest had a baby in her 70s.

00:25:33.140 --> 00:25:36.820
Well, we got a couple of decades on her.

00:25:38.760 --> 00:25:40.660
We could try, if you want.

00:25:42.680 --> 00:25:43.060
Really?

00:25:50.590 --> 00:25:52.580
But, here you go.

00:25:53.090 --> 00:25:54.280
Yes, thank you.

00:25:54.700 --> 00:25:56.610
Uh, do you need me for anything else?

00:25:56.650 --> 00:25:57.430
No, that should be all.

00:25:57.550 --> 00:25:57.950
Thank you, Louise.

00:26:04.700 --> 00:26:08.130
I wonder when's the best time to start trying again.

00:26:09.760 --> 00:26:10.740
I'm free tonight.

00:26:11.870 --> 00:26:12.770
Sounds good to me.

00:26:14.080 --> 00:26:16.520
Well, I see no visible fractures.

00:26:17.360 --> 00:26:18.520
I wish the resolution was better.

00:26:19.680 --> 00:26:21.750
We'll set up a scan, just to be certain.

00:26:22.210 --> 00:26:23.010
Much better detail.

00:26:23.390 --> 00:26:24.210
Whatever you think.

00:26:25.220 --> 00:26:26.440
I'd better get home and start dinner.

00:26:27.260 --> 00:26:27.840
Will you be home?

00:26:28.960 --> 00:26:29.980
Uh, just have some paper.

00:26:30.770 --> 00:26:32.140
I'll be right behind you.

00:26:43.290 --> 00:26:43.750
Oh, God.

00:26:44.520 --> 00:26:44.940
I know.

00:26:45.140 --> 00:26:45.740
This is amazing.

00:26:46.650 --> 00:26:47.410
It's like she's magic.

00:26:47.690 --> 00:26:47.910
Hmm.

00:26:50.290 --> 00:26:50.950
So what am I doing?

00:26:51.150 --> 00:26:51.470
Right?

00:26:52.540 --> 00:26:52.720
Okay.

00:26:53.020 --> 00:26:53.240
I understand.

00:26:53.540 --> 00:26:54.480
But you were thinking it.

00:26:56.460 --> 00:26:57.020
I don't know, man.

00:26:57.080 --> 00:26:58.040
I don't know what the hell happened.

00:26:58.200 --> 00:26:58.800
I'll tell you what happened.

00:26:58.860 --> 00:26:59.980
Your brother came here and decided...

00:27:00.000 --> 00:27:05.740
to stir the pot that's what families do that's what makes the holidays so fun i know and i knew

00:27:05.740 --> 00:27:09.180
brian would pull this crap he always does i just didn't think i'd be so susceptible to it

00:27:09.340 --> 00:27:17.890
i thought i was happy huh you seem happy well maybe i'm not i mean if i was wouldn't i be more

00:27:17.890 --> 00:27:22.770
sure about everything no not necessarily you know i got the same pitch when i first got here

00:27:22.770 --> 00:27:29.010
you're crazy you're gonna miss the city you'll never last a year i heard them all so what made

00:27:29.010 --> 00:27:29.650
you stop listening.

00:27:30.670 --> 00:27:34.620
I don't know. It wasn't any great epiphany or anything.

00:27:34.820 --> 00:27:35.580
Maybe Brian's right.

00:27:35.990 --> 00:27:40.040
I mean, maybe I do need to spend half my day alone on a freeway to be happy.

00:27:40.260 --> 00:27:41.020
